{"text": "Gus Bauman Robert R. Harris\n\nBeveridge & Diamond, P.C. Lerch, Early & Brewer\n1350 I Street, NW 3 Bethesda Metro Center\nSuite 700 Suite 460\nWashington, DC 20005 Bethesda, MD 20814\nDecember 3, 2013\n\nThe Honorable Nancy Navarro\nPresident\nMontgomery County Council\nStella B. Werner Council Office Building\n100 Maryland Avenue, 6th Floor\nRockville, MD 20850\n\nRe: Ten Mile Creek Area Limited Amendment \u2014 Clarksburg Master Plan\n\nDear Council President Navarro and Councilmembers:\n\nWe represent Pulte Homes Inc. (\u201cPulte\u201d) with respect to property it owns and has under\ncontract within the Ten Mile Creek Area of Clarksburg. The purpose of this letter is to inform\nthe County Council of significant legal issues concerning the Draft Master Plan Amendment and\nits treatment of Pulte. By separate letter, the engineering and water quality experts engaged by\nPulte will be submitting detailed scientific data and comprehensive analyses with respect to\ndevelopment of the property and the recommendations within the Draft Master Plan\nAmendment. This will include specific information detailing flaws in the analyses undertaken\nby the Maryland-National Capital Park and Planning Commission (\u201cM-NCPPC\u201d) and its\nconsultants that have led to their unjustified recommendations of changes to the Master Plan and\nzoning currently in effect.\n\nOur legal claims identified in this letter are based, in part, on the information and material\nbeing submitted in that second letter as well as by the extensive record in the Master Plan review\nprocess by M-NCPPC. The information and arguments contained in these various sources\nconvey a compelling justification either to leave the current Master Plan recommendations and\nzoning applicable to the Pulte properties in place, or to limit any changes to those that would\nenable Pulte to develop its property in a manner substantially similar to the current Master Plan\nrecommendations.\n\nIn this letter, we briefly discuss six critical points in which we believe the Planning Board\n\nDraft Master Plan, and the flawed studies on which it is based, violate Pulte\u2019s Constitutional and\nother property rights, including the following:\n\n1612144.1 85247.003",
